<ontology/use_pharmaceuticals/use_pharmaceuticals__0750__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 256" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n256> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cream of Tartar used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 256"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CREAM OF TARTAR: (GER. Weinsteinrahm. DU. Wynsteenroom. DA. Wynsteenflöde. SW. Winstenflötor. FR. Crème de tartre. IT. Crema di tartaro. SP. Creemor tartaro. PORT. Creemor de tartaro. LAT. Creemor tartari,) called also crystals of tartar, is a preparation of tartar, and comes to us from Leghorn, and other parts of Italy. It is a combination of tartaric acid ..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
